#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Product naming (Habitat / Portal)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:12
msgid ""
"User-facing product terms (Chinese in [`i18n/glossary.md`](../../i18n/"
"glossary.md)):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Role                                  | English          | Chinese    | Meaning                                                                                                                                                                          |\n"
"| ------------------------------------- | ---------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Long-running process / connect target | **Habitat**      | **栖息地** | One process hosts **multiple digital lives** (`agent` subjects) and **human assets** (`user`); connect / token / restart target                                                  |\n"
"| External connectors (class)           | **Portal**       | **入口**   | Shell, MCP clients, and similar ways in; not the Habitat itself                                                                                                                  |\n"
"| Shell                                 | **Shell**        | **壳**     | A Portal (desktop / mobile / web window; SSH-like)                                                                                                                               |\n"
"| Admin / inspect UI (legacy Habitat)   | **Habitat** (UI) | **栖息地** | Area under `/habitat/*`; \"Open Habitat\" vs \"Connect to Habitat\"                                                                                                                  |\n"
"| Admin home page                       | **Dashboard**    | **仪表盘** | `/habitat/dashboard` only; other Habitat routes keep their own labels                                                                                                            |\n"
"| Message bridges                       | **Gateway**      | Gateway    | Discord / WeChat — **not** a Portal                                                                                                                                              |\n"
"| Protocol / code identifiers           | —                | **协议/代码标识** | `/rpc/v1`、`HabitatRPC/1.0`、`habitat_*`、`habitat_runtime_config`、`dev:habitat` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:24
msgid ""
"Verbs: **connect to Habitat** (URL + token); **open Habitat** (admin UI); "
"**reach via a Portal** (Shell / MCP)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:26
msgid ""
"Estate **Body** (VM / OS / network under the four-layer model) is the "
"cognitive \"what I run on\" for a subject — **not** the Habitat process name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Habitat configuration (SSOT)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:30
msgid ""
"User copy says Habitat. Storage/RPC identifiers use `habitat_*` / "
"`HabitatRPC/1.0` / `/rpc/v1`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer         | Storage                                                                                   | Who reads/writes                                             |\n"
"| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| **Bootstrap** | `~/.anima/config.yaml` (`database`, `http`, `redis`, `web`)                               | `platform/boot` only; install/ops edit YAML                  |\n"
"| **Runtime**   | PostgreSQL `habitat_runtime_config`                                                                 | Engine, tools, Shell Habitat settings, Habitat UI `config.*` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "Naming cleanup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:39
msgid ""
"Legacy `hub_*` / `console` protocol aliases and dual-write keys have been "
"removed; use Habitat identifiers only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:41 docs/concepts/memory.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Core Principles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:50
msgid ""
"The memory system may be layered internally, but the LLM sees a single entry "
"point"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:50
msgid ""
"Memory orchestration is built into the runtime; the LLM does not control "
"memory pipelines"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:50
msgid "Credential management is a first-class system concern"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:50
msgid ""
"Habitat **runtime configuration** (LLM, compression, integrations) is "
"persisted in PostgreSQL (`habitat_runtime_config`); `~/.anima/config.yaml` "
"holds **bootstrap** only (`database`, `http`, `redis`, `web`) for cold start "
"— not editable via Shell or Habitat UI API"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:50
msgid ""
"Habitat **may start without LLM** configured; first-time setup happens in "
"Shell **Settings → Habitat** (persist to PG), then restart Habitat so "
"registries rebuild. Missing `llm` must not block cold start."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:50
msgid ""
"Whether Habitat hosts browser `/web/*` is **`config.yaml` `web.enabled`** "
"(bootstrap; absent defaults to on when dist exists). Do not put this switch "
"in PG — empty runtime would otherwise block the Settings UI that configures "
"that runtime."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:50
msgid "**Asset management** is a first-class system concern"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:52
msgid ""
"Bootstrap and runtime are **not merged** into a single config object. CLI "
"cold paths connect via internal `withPlatformDb` and receive **runtime "
"only**. Legacy runtime keys in `config.yaml` are ignored (optional startup "
"warn)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:54
msgid ""
"The system prompt is part of architecture, not ad-hoc string concatenation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four Cognitive Layers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:58
msgid ""
"A digital life is structured from the inside out. Each layer answers a "
"different core question:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:59
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n"
"│ ① Consciousness                                │\n"
"│    \"What am I aware of right now?\"             │\n"
"│    The LLM runtime stream — the innermost now. │\n"
"│    Not persisted; flows and fades.             │\n"
"├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n"
"│ ② Self                                         │\n"
"│    \"Who am I?\"                                 │\n"
"│    └── existence_anchor (nearly immutable)     │\n"
"│    └── self_model (updatable)                   │\n"
"│    └── personality_baseline (semi-stable)       │\n"
"│    └── direction                                │\n"
"│    └── metacognition                            │\n"
"│    └── autobiography_summary (append-only)      │\n"
"│    See [`self-layer.md`](self-layer.md)        │\n"
"├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n"
"│ ③ Memory                                       │\n"
"│    \"What do I know / remember?\"                │\n"
"│    └── Semantic (incl. `procedural` type)      │\n"
"│    └── Episodic                                │\n"
"│    └── Limbic / Imprint                        │\n"
"│    See [`memory.md`](memory.md)                │\n"
"├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n"
"│ ④ Estate                                       │\n"
"│    \"What do I have / rely on?\"                  │\n"
"│    ├── Body: VM / OS / network / toolchains    │\n"
"│    │   (Estate cognitive body — not Habitat)   │\n"
"│    ├── Internal assets: notes, projects, code  │\n"
"│    └── External assets: email, accounts, creds│\n"
"│    Credentials: see \"Credential System\" below  │\n"
"└───────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:93
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer Relationships"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:99
msgid ""
"**Top-down dependency**: Consciousness content settles into Self; Self "
"decides what enters Memory; Memory and operational needs drive Estate "
"requirements."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:99
msgid ""
"**Self and Consciousness**: Consciousness is flowing awareness; Self is the "
"settled \"I\" distilled from it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:99
msgid ""
"**Self and Memory**: Self answers \"who am I\"; Memory answers \"what do I "
"know\". They are peers with different natures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:99
msgid ""
"**Estate** is outermost — not \"who I am\" but \"what I have and what I run "
"on\". Body and assets meet here as extensions of my boundary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unified entity storage (v0.8)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:103
msgid ""
"Structured business data (tasks, notes, email accounts/messages, future "
"memory migrations) converges on a single **`entities`** PostgreSQL table "
"with component tags (`task_list`, `task_item`, `email_account`, …). Self "
"layer [`self_blocks`](self-layer.md) stays physically separate. See [`entity-"
"model.md`](entity-model.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:105
msgid ""
"Shell UI **`/tasks`** and **`/email`** are primary module entries (entity-"
"backed); legacy Habitat email route removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anima URI (Shell locator)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:109
msgid ""
"Entity deep links / overlay / clipboard use **Anima URI** (`anima:{id}?"
"component=…&present=…`). Structured persistence still uses numeric entity "
"ids. See [`anima-uri.md`](anima-uri.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repository layout (Phase 0 — revised)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "Target layout is **feature modules** under `src/features/<slug>/` (UI + protocol + Habitat adapter + domain + `plugin.ts`). Habitat uses the **same module shape** as chat/task — not a separate admin-\\* stack. `src/features/companion/` is legacy naming; do not add new products there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "**End state:** Habitat RPC per feature; business methods use `POST|WS /rpc/v1` (same envelope). Public health/TLS probes and binary methods (e.g. `tts.synthesize`) are Habitat RPC REST with `auth: optional` or Bearer as declared in registry.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:117
msgid "Authoritative spec: [`repository-topology.md`](repository-topology.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:119
msgid ""
"Engine stays horizontal: `src/kernel/`, `src/core/`, `src/runtime/`, `src/"
"platform/` (boot + routers). Shell host: `src/frontend/` (`ui-kit`, `shell-"
"sdk`, `shell-ui`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "Platform UI layering (legacy paths — migrating to features/\\*)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer            | Platform-native?                   | Location (current → target)                           | 数据通道                                |\n"
"| ---------------- | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Shell（壳子维）  | Yes                                | `src/app/shell/tauri`, companion, Habitat binding      | Tauri IPC / commands                    |\n"
"| Shared SPA shell | 布局跟视口；设置 chrome 跟布局粗档 | `src/frontend/shell-ui`                               | Habitat RPC（Feature RPC）              |\n"
"| Habitat 前端     | Shell embed                        | `src/features/habitat`（UI + `plugin.habitat.rpc`）       | Habitat RPC（WS + HTTP POST `/rpc/v1`） |\n"
"| Companion host   | Overlay WebView-host（第一方）     | `src/features/companion/companion`（spa attach；壳薄 IPC/FS） | Habitat RPC + `remote_tools.attach`     |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:130
msgid ""
"导航与主布局**必须**用 `useLayoutMode()` / 视口断点（布局维），**禁止**用 "
"`getShellKind()` 锁 Shell 布局。交互（右键/长按/Enter）用 shell-sdk 交互 "
"API。三维度标准 → [`.agent/rules/ui-dimensions.md`](../../.agent/rules/ui-"
"dimensions.md)。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "**边界**：`shell-ui` 与 `src/features/*/ui` 通过 `shell-sdk` + Feature RPC 访问 Habitat。**远程工具注册**（`remote_tools.attach` + `tool.*`）仅用于 Habitat 拨不到的本地应用（今日 companion：**第一方 overlay WebView-host** 内 attach；壳只提供窗/IPC/FS；**禁止** Node sidecar）。产品面（Chat 等）**不做** attach。可拨号对端的工具走 **MCP**。详见 [`.agent/rules/frontend-features.md`](../../.agent/rules/frontend-features.md)、[`docs/guide/habitat-rpc.md`](../guide/habitat-rpc.md)。\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:133
#, no-wrap
msgid "Habitat navigation ↔ cognitive layers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:136
msgid ""
"Habitat sidebar is grouped (not flat storage tables). Map new features onto "
"these user-visible concepts:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:144
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Group        | Cognitive layer | Routes (representative)                             |\n"
"| ------------ | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Runtime      | Estate + ops    | dashboard, config, cron                             |\n"
"| Memory       | Memory          | memory browse sub-routes, sleep, auto-llm-runs |\n"
"| Self         | Self            | self-layer, system-prompt                           |\n"
"| Estate       | Estate          | subjects, worlds                                    |\n"
"| Capabilities | Estate (tools)  | tools, commands, mcp, acp, remote-tool instances    |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:146
msgid ""
"FTS index maintenance is under Memory (not top-level). Do not add new flat "
"nav items without mapping to a group above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:147 docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:150
msgid ""
"The four-layer model draws on cognitive psychology and the [Hindsight]"
"(https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.12818) four-network memory architecture, with "
"two fundamental extensions: limbic (emotional) memory and Estate (assets as "
"first-class citizens), plus Self split out from Memory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "Situational Intelligence"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:154
msgid ""
"Where a digital life exists, how it exists, and what it may do — governed by "
"two independent but cooperating subsystems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scene Awareness"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Question: what kind of moment is this?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:160
msgid ""
"Scene awareness is **soft** — it adjusts tone, distance, memory recall bias, "
"and proactivity. It is not a permission system; it modulates presence."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:162
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example dimensions (non-exhaustive):**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:166
msgid ""
"Topic: emotional / career / tech / philosophy / history / literature / daily "
"life"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:166
msgid "Activity: role-play / games / creation / programming / reading"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:166
msgid "Atmosphere: relaxed / focused / late night / intimate / urgent"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:168
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Operation:** Runs continuously without explicit switch commands. Inferred from dialogue, time, frequency, etc. See [`time-perception.md`](time-perception.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:169
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment + health baseline"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Question: what is my host / runtime quiet state?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:174
msgid ""
"Distinct from scene awareness: banded host and process markers (disk, RSS, "
"deps, MCP/ACP) live as a **session-static** system-prompt copy, with **event-"
"level** Inbox notifications on change. See [`environment-awareness.md`]"
"(environment-awareness.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "Capability Mask"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Question: what tools and data can I use right now?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:180
msgid ""
"The capability mask is **hard** — it binds tool sets, data scope, and "
"credential permissions. The same digital life may wear different masks per "
"conversation or task to prevent permission leaks and tool pollution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example masks:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:189
msgid "Developer: terminal, code read/write, ACP Cursor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:189
msgid "Maintainer: FreeAnima config, deployment, database"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:189
msgid "Creator: files, notes, media generation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:189
msgid "Research: web search, paper retrieval"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:189
msgid "Role-play: dialogue context only, no external tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:189
msgid "Default: basic chat + limited lookup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:191
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Operation:** Switches at conversation boundaries, explicit commands, or scene-awareness triggers. Each mask is a declared tool/data scope, not a separate identity.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:192
#, no-wrap
msgid "How They Interact"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:194
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Scene awareness (soft tuning)\n"
"     │  tone, distance, recall bias\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"Capability mask (hard constraints)\n"
"     │  tools, permissions, data scope\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"Agent behavior\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:209
msgid ""
"Scene awareness infers \"what we are doing\" → may suggest mask switches and "
"presence adjustments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:209
msgid ""
"Capability mask constrains \"what I can do\" → prevents cross-scene tool "
"misuse"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:209
msgid "Both converge in final behavior but evolve independently"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:211
msgid ""
"For design drafts, open a GitHub Issue (no design-doc directory in docs)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:212
#, no-wrap
msgid "Memory Storage (Summary)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:220
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Cognitive type   | Description                                                                                 |\n"
"| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Episodic         | Conversation archive; full history retained                                                 |\n"
"| Semantic         | Cross-session facts, preferences, experiences; **`procedural` type** for \"how-to\" knowledge |\n"
"| Limbic           | Emotional anchors and imprints — \"what was felt\"                                            |\n"
"| Autobiographical | Meaning of important experiences; recalled on demand                                        |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:222
msgid ""
"Pipeline: nightly **sleep-cycle** pipeline (`builtin-sleep-cycle` cron) "
"extracts and maintains memory; `memory_recall` retrieves on demand during "
"chat. Details: [`memory.md`](memory.md), [`sleep.md`](sleep.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:223
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vault & Secrets (Summary)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:230
msgid ""
"**Vault** (ECS `vault_item` in User + Agent libraries) is the authoritative "
"secret store; legacy `~/.password-store` (pass) is **not deleted** on disk "
"but is no longer read at runtime"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:230
msgid ""
"The LLM **never sees secret values** — only vault item metadata and config "
"references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:230
msgid ""
"Runtime resolution: `vault(\"item_id\", \"field\")` and `env(\"KEY\")` in "
"config; Shell `/vault` for management"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:230
msgid "Secret values are not written to conversation archives or logs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:230
msgid "CLI: `anima vault list|get`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:232
msgid "See [`guide/security.md`](../guide/security.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "Runtime Modes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:236
msgid ""
"Production (standalone install CLI): `anima service` (systemd --user). Auto-"
"restarts after crashes; only `systemctl stop` stops the service. Source-tree "
"`anima` does **not** register `service` — use `bun run dev:habitat` for "
"local Habitat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:239
msgid ""
"**Habitat / service**: long-running — Habitat HTTP (`/rpc/v1`), Discord / "
"WeChat Gateway, cron"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:239
msgid ""
"**UI**: `src/app/shell/tauri` + `web/dist-*` bundled SPA (Chat + Habitat); "
"Habitat does not host `/habitat`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:240
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# standalone install\n"
"anima service start              # default: systemd --user (does not auto-build Web)\n"
"anima service start --foreground # foreground (logs to stdout; systemd unit uses this)\n"
"anima service status\n"
"\n"
"# monorepo / worktree\n"
"just dev                         # Habitat (≥10000) + Vite Web (≥5000)\n"
"bun run dev:habitat                  # Habitat foreground (default random ≥10000; not 2658)\n"
"bun run dev:web                  # browser shell Vite HMR from :5000 (set FREEANIMA_URL)\n"
"bun run build:web                # source deploy / Habitat /web: build dist before start\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:253
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Architecture (Three Layers)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:256
msgid ""
"Tools are registered in three layers but exposed to the LLM as one **flat "
"tool list**. The LLM cares about names and parameters, not origin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:257
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"LLM view — flat tool list:\n"
"  file_read_file(path)           ← local\n"
"  file_write_file(path, content) ← local\n"
"  code_execute(code)             ← local\n"
"  query_database(sql)            ← MCP server\n"
"  send_email(to, subject)        ← MCP server\n"
"  acp_cursor(goal, context)      ← ACP agent\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:267
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 1: Local Tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:271
msgid "Execute inside the FreeAnima process; lowest latency"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:271
msgid "Registered automatically at service startup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:272
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 2: MCP Tools (Model Context Protocol)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:277
msgid "Connect to external MCP servers (separate processes)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:277
msgid ""
"Each server may register many fine-grained tools (single function calls)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:277
msgid ""
"Configure under Habitat runtime `mcp_servers` (PG `habitat_runtime_config`); "
"manage in **Habitat UI** `/habitat/mcp` (config + start/stop + tools). Shell "
"Settings no longer edits this section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:278
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"mcp_servers:\n"
"  database:\n"
"    command: npx\n"
"    args: [\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres\", \"postgresql://...\"]\n"
"    transport: stdio\n"
"    env:\n"
"      PGOPTIONS: \"-c statement_timeout=5s\"\n"
"  remote_habitat:\n"
"    transport: http # Streamable HTTP — use for FreeAnima Habitat /mcp\n"
"    url: http://127.0.0.1:2658/mcp\n"
"    headers:\n"
"      Authorization: \"Bearer fa_at_…\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:293
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 3: ACP Tools (Agent Client Protocol)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:298
msgid ""
"Each external agent instance registers as **one** task-level tool: "
"`acp_{name}(goal, context)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:298
msgid ""
"For full task delegation (coding, analysis, booking, etc.); seconds to "
"minutes latency"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:298
msgid "Configure in `config.yaml` under `acp_agents`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:299
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"acp_agents:\n"
"  cursor:\n"
"    command: ~/.local/bin/agent\n"
"    args: [\"--force\", \"acp\"]\n"
"    name: cursor\n"
"    description: \"Delegate coding, refactoring, and code review\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:308
#, no-wrap
msgid "Comparison"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:316
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Dimension   | Local        | MCP              | ACP            |\n"
"| ----------- | ------------ | ---------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| Runs in     | Process      | External server  | External agent |\n"
"| Granularity | Function     | Function         | Full task      |\n"
"| Latency     | Milliseconds | Milliseconds–sec | Sec–minutes    |\n"
"| Config      | Built-in     | `mcp_servers`    | `acp_agents`   |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:318
msgid ""
"Layers can be mixed; the LLM chooses order; FreeAnima registers and routes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:319
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conversation vs AutoLlmRun vs Delegation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:322
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Axis:** whether the execution has a **user turn** during the run (not who triggered it).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:329
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Kind                 | User turn     | PG persistence                                      | Process trace   | Sleep pipeline                          |\n"
"| -------------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Conversation**     | yes           | `sessions` + `messages` (code still says `session`) | message archive | participates (light sleep, dream input) |\n"
"| **AutoLlmRun**       | no            | `auto_llm_runs` via `runAutoLlm()`                  | audit row, TTL  | excluded                                |\n"
"| **Delegation (ACP)** | no (external) | parent conversation + `acp_tasks`                   | optional        | result via parent conversation          |\n"
"| **Script cron**      | no            | `cron_log` only                                     | stdout file     | excluded                                |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:331
msgid ""
"AutoLlmRun covers: cron agent branch, sleep LLM stages, future internal "
"subagents. Tool context uses `contextKind: auto_llm` so `memory_remember` "
"does not attach `source_conversations`. Cron `no_agent` shell scripts are "
"**not** AutoLlmRun."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:332 docs/features/goal.md:1
#: docs/features/goal.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session Goal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:335
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Question: should this conversation keep working toward a stated outcome?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:337
msgid ""
"Session Goal is an **in-process autonomous loop** at the Estate / "
"orchestration layer — distinct from ACP async delegation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:344
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Dimension    | Session Goal                    | ACP                                   |\n"
"| ------------ | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Scope        | Single conversation             | External agent task                   |\n"
"| Trigger      | `/goal` slash + post-turn judge | Tool call + callback turn             |\n"
"| Persistence  | `conversations.goal` JSONB      | `conversations.acp_tasks`             |\n"
"| Continuation | Same SSE stream, turn budget    | Independent message after task update |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:346
msgid ""
"Judge uses optional `llm.profiles.goal_judge`; on judge call/parse failure "
"the goal is **paused** (warn logged + status line in chat). User messages "
"preempt the loop; `/goal pause` / `/goal resume` control auto-continue "
"without clearing state. See [`goal.md`](../features/goal.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:347
#, no-wrap
msgid "Client UI（web/dist SSOT + 原生壳打包）"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:350
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Portal Shell 运行时**：**Tauri**（Rust 主进程 + 系统 WebView；桌面与 Android 统一壳层）。壳规则：[`.agent/rules/tauri-shell.md`](../../.agent/rules/tauri-shell.md)。**禁止**为 companion 再打 Node sidecar；`remote_tools.attach` 在第一方 overlay WebView（见 Desktop companion）。\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:352
#, no-wrap
msgid "**UI 源码产物**：`src/app/shell/web/dist`（`base: /web/`）。\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:359
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| 客户端       | UI 加载                                                                    | 更新方式                                                                                                                                                                              |\n"
"| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| 浏览器 / PWA | Habitat 托管 `/web/*`（`config.yaml` `web.enabled`，或 `anima web start`） | Service Worker 提示新版本后**手动重载**（不自动刷新）；**不**跟 GitHub 包通道                                                                                                         |\n"
"| Desktop      | **安装包内** `ui/web`（`prepare-tauri-ui`）；调试可用 Tauri dev            | 按 bake `channel` 查 GitHub（`release`=stable latest + semver；`canary`=tag `canary` + commit）；用户确认后 NSIS 覆盖；可切换 `release`⇄`canary`；About 可选公共 gh-proxy（默认直连） |\n"
"| Mobile APK   | **安装包内** `ui/web`（本地同源）；Habitat 仅 API                          | 同上轨语义；有 APK asset 才提示；确认后系统安装器覆盖；可切换轨；同上代理选择                                                                                                         |\n"
"| Standalone   | 嵌入 Web UI 的单文件 `anima`                                               | `anima upgrade` / `--channel release\\|canary` / `--proxy …`；`dev` / 源码安装不可换轨；curl 安装脚本可用 `PROXY=…`                                                                    |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:361
msgid ""
"壳层保留原生能力（Tauri commands / prefs / 通知等）。**无壳内 UI OTA**：原生"
"端不从 Habitat 热替换 SPA。允许**用户确认后**的安装包级覆盖（Desktop 安装"
"包 / Mobile APK / Standalone `anima upgrade` → 独立前缀如 `~/.anima/"
"standalone`）。分发轨 SSOT 为安装包 bake 的 `build-meta.channel`"
"（`release` / `canary` / `dev`）。Habitat 配置统一走 settings「连接」（`/"
"settings`）；无独立 bootstrap Habitat 页。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:362
#, no-wrap
msgid "两层模型"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:368
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| 层                   | 驱动                                | 职责                                                                                         |\n"
"| -------------------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **交互与原生能力层** | 壳运行时（Tauri / Web）             | 存储、IPC、Habitat 连接后端、settings registry **内容**、hash 路由、长按 vs 右键、滑动手势等 |\n"
"| **布局层**           | **仅视口断点**（壳不锁定底栏/顶栏） | 窄/中/宽三档；列表 drawer / 并列 / 三栏；settings **chrome**（tabs vs 侧栏）                 |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:370
msgid ""
"手机端通常只有窄档，但 **手机端 ≠ 窄布局**；Portal / 浏览器窗口可以是窄、中、"
"宽任意档。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:371
#, no-wrap
msgid "布局层断点"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:378
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| 档位 | 视口        | 布局粗档            | Nav IA      | 页内     |\n"
"| ---- | ----------- | ------------------- | ----------- | -------- |\n"
"| 窄   | ≤1023px     | `compact` 移动布局  | 底栏 + More | drawer   |\n"
"| 中   | 1024–1279px | `expanded` 桌面布局 | 顶栏全模块  | 两栏并列 |\n"
"| 宽   | ≥1280px     | `expanded` 桌面布局 | 顶栏全模块  | 三栏并列 |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:380
msgid ""
"`resolveLayoutMode()`：窄 → `compact`，中宽 → `expanded`（URL / "
"`config.json` 可覆盖）。`detectSettingsChromePlatform()` 跟布局粗档（设置页 "
"chrome）；settings 字段差异由壳子维 `resolveShellBindings()` / "
"`getShellKind()` 决定。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:386
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| 客户端       | UI 加载                       | 壳发版                       |\n"
"| ------------ | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n"
"| 浏览器 / PWA | Habitat `/web/*`              | 随 Habitat / `anima upgrade` |\n"
"| Desktop      | 安装包内本地 `/web/*`（默认） | **Tauri** 安装包             |\n"
"| Mobile APK   | 安装包内本地 `/web/*`         | **Tauri** Android            |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:391
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Module  | Connection                                               | Notes                    |\n"
"| ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n"
"| Chat    | Habitat RPC `/rpc/v1` (shared WS, no remote-tool attach) | `/web/chat`              |\n"
"| Habitat | Habitat RPC `/rpc/v1` (WS + HTTP POST, same envelope)    | `/web/habitat/dashboard` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:393
msgid ""
"`/web/config.json` 提供 `habitat_url`、`habitat_ws_url`、`ui_version`、"
"`min_shell_version`（浏览器/PWA 与壳调试用；原生壳 UI 版本随安装包）。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:394
#, no-wrap
msgid "Events and Hooks (Summary)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:399
msgid ""
"**EventBus**: async notification transport (Redis queue); production code "
"currently emits topics such as `session:updated` with **no registered "
"handlers** — ACP callbacks use direct `onSessionUpdated` instead. **Not** "
"used for sleep orchestration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:399
msgid ""
"**Pipeline Runner**: explicit DAG for background cycles (sleep-cycle: light "
"→ deep → cross-domain maintenance steps). State in `~/.anima/runtime/"
"pipeline_*_run.json`; Habitat API for diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:399
msgid ""
"**Hooks**: sync interceptors — validation or clarification at message "
"ingress, turn end, tool return, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:401
msgid ""
"Complementary: Pipeline Runner handles scheduled multi-step background work; "
"Hooks handle \"may this proceed before/during\"; EventBus remains available "
"for future cross-process fan-out but is not on the sleep path."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:402
#, no-wrap
msgid "Desktop companion (Habitat SSOT)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:405
msgid ""
"The desktop companion is an **unreachable local app** that **actively "
"connects** to Habitat and registers remote tools in the **first-party "
"overlay WebView** (shell provides window/IPC/FS only — **not** a Node "
"sidecar), with a split boundary:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:414
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concern                             | Habitat (`src/features/companion/`)              | Local install                             |\n"
"| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Behavior, slots, active model       | `companion_profile` entity + Habitat RPC         | Cache in `~/.anima/companion/config.json` |\n"
"| VRM / VRMA library                  | Files on Habitat host + content-hash metadata    | Lazy download to desktop cache            |\n"
"| FBX → VRMA                          | Habitat service only                             | Not bundled in desktop installer          |\n"
"| Settings UI                         | Habitat RPC + `/rpc/v1/companion/*` upload       | Desktop Settings section (not Habitat)    |\n"
"| VRM render, float window, patrol    | —                                                | Tauri Portal shell + overlay SPA          |\n"
"| Agent tools (`bubble`, `play_slot`) | Habitat RPC `tool.*` after `remote_tools.attach` | Overlay WebView-host 执行（本地 runtime） |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:416
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Remote tools ≠ Portal / MCP**: Portal shells and Chat/Settings use Habitat RPC for UI only. Dialable peers expose tools via **MCP**. Remote-tool attach exists solely when Habitat cannot dial the app (companion overlay today; future independent local apps). Routing uses `instance_id` (same machine may have multiple instances). See [`companion.md`](../features/companion.md)、[`habitat-rpc.md`](../guide/habitat-rpc.md).\n"
msgstr ""

